                                    PRESENTS

                      QuickNew V2.2 coded by CALYPSO/GOD !
                      
                              Updated by REbEL/QTX 

    PROFESSIONAL TOOLS FOR PROFESSIONAL SYSOPS - GET THE REAL QUALITY !


WHAT'S THE USE OF THIS TOOL ?
-----------------------------

        This tool creates a textfile which includes all filenames
        today uploaded in every (selected) conference !

        It creates a nice Ansi-Output which you can display
        after the Logonscreen or after the Lastcallers (look for
        examples how to do this later in this docs) !

        Another possibility is to make bulls for each conference !

        It's very nice to get a quick overview of all new files.
        Also the users can see if there are new files in a conference
        which has not every day new files !

        Gives many additional informations, like Number of Files and
        Fakes, total Megs for today and yesterday (configurable) !

        Ofcourse it's another high-quality tool from me, 100% written
        in Assembler for maximum speed !
        
        ... and it's the fastest/best-looking one !!!

  .-----------------------------------------------------------------------.
  |       PLEASE READ THE REGISTER!.TXT INCLUDED IN THIS ARCHIVE !!!      |
  `-----------------------------------------------------------------------'

HOW TO INSTALL :
----------------

        First you have to edit your Config-File(s) !
        (I use S:QuickNew.Config(x) !)

        The first line of the Config-File includes the Prefix
        displayed for every normal filename (normally a colour-code,
        like [0m) !

        The second line includes the Prefix displayed for every
        deleted (nuked) file !!! So can show your nuked files
        in RED or some other colour ! (I use [35m)

        (The tool detects deleted files with the 'D' in the Dirfile, so
         be sure to use a Faker which supports this, e.g. Amifaker !)

        The third line is the DisplayMode ! There are three available :

        1 - Normal Displaymode   : All Files are shown right after
                                   each other.

        2 - Columns Displaymode  : The Files will be shown in columns
                                   (my prefered one !)

        3 - Centered Displaymode : The Lines with the Files will be
                                   shown centered ! (also nice)


    ->  Now you write down the text you want to display ! You can write
    |   there what you want ! The end of your text must be marked with
    |   a line only including a '#' !
    |
    |   After the text you give the full path + name of your upload-dirfile
    |   of the corresponding conference !
    |
    ---- repeat this to show multiple Conferences !


        Special Features :
        ------------------

        You can include special keywords in your text, these are :

        @N      Number of todays files...    
        @F      Number of todays fakes...    
        @Y      Number of yesterdays files...
        @Z      Number of yesterdays fakes...
        @M.0    Todays Megs uploaded !       
        @B.0    Yesterdays Megs uploaded !
        @D      Number of days of data to process (eg instead of yesterday
                and today it can be last 7 days and previous 7 days.

        Take a look at the included examples and change them to your
        needs !
        Here's also an example :

----------------------------(cut here)--------
[0m
[35m
2

[32mLast @D Days Uploads in [33m>> Amiga Forever <<[34m :      [0m([35mFiles[33m: [36m@N[0m, [35mFakes[33m: [36m@F, [35mMegs[33m: [36m@M.0[0m)
[35mYesterdays Statistics [0m: [32m@Y [36mFiles[33m, [32m@Z [36mFakes[33m, [32m@B.0 [36mMegs [33m![0m
#
BBS:Conf02/Dir1
[32mTodays Uploads in [33m>> Console Corner <<[34m :      [0m([35mFiles[33m: [36m@N[0m, [35mFakes[33m: [36m@F, [35mMegs[33m: [36m@M.0[0m)
[35mYesterdays Statistics [0m: [32m@Y [36mFiles[33m, [32m@Z [36mFakes[33m, [32m@B.0 [36mMegs [33m![0m
#
BBS:Conf03/Dir1
----------------------------(cut here)--------

        
        You can run the tool from CLI for testing. The output
        will be sent to your CLI-Window. Install it in your
        Logoff-Batch using '>' to redirect the output to a file !
        
        You can also specify the number of days of data to process.
        This is a new parameter for V2.2 - prior to this it was only
        able to process yesterday and today. This is equivalant to
        passing in 1 (which is also the default for backwards compatbility).
        Passing in 7 for example will display 7 the last 7 days of files and
        a further 7 days of stats.

        E.g. :

        ----------------------------(cut here)--------
        QuickNew S:QuickNew.Config 7 >BBS:Screens/QuickNew.txt.gr
        ----------------------------(cut here)--------

        There is also a limitation that however many days of files you specify
        they must all exist in the single directory file you specify in the config
        file. It wont scan to previous directory files, in addition it will only process
        a maximum of the last 80000 bytes of the directory file for each conference.

        If you call it with different config-files you can make
        different outputs, e.g. for every conference !

        Example-Outputs are included in the archive !


        Now some hints how you can display it in your BBS !

        This is my Node(x)/Bull(x).txt(.gr) :

        ----------------------------(cut here)--------
        ~SS_BBS:Screens/LastCallers.txt.gr
        ~SP                               
        ~SS_BBS:Screens/QuickNew.txt.gr
        ----------------------------(cut here)--------

        So you can display the Lastcallers and the QuickNew right
        after each other...        


